WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:05.130
Forget your cape heroes and austere prestige
dramas the most auspicious franchise season

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:05.980
is here again.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:10.400
The Fast Saga has blessed us with a trailer
for its latest iteration, the ninth Fast and

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.660
Furious film, aptly titled F9.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:15.040
There's more to the trailer than meets the
eye.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.500
It's impossible to talk about the F9 trailer
and not talk about Han Lue.

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:23.500
If you're a casual viewer of the Fast and
Furious franchise or you're still catching

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:25.820
up on it, you might need some context.

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:29.920
The end of the trailer features a Korean man
walking in and munching on a snack.

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:34.640
That would be Han Lue, played by Sung Kang,
who has presumably been recovering from getting

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:36.060
killed in an earlier movie.

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:40.860
Han is at the center of a mildly confusing
timeline shift that the Fast and Furious franchise

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:43.300
made as it was hitting the metaphorical NOS
button.

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:47.750
The character was introduced and subsequently
died in what appears to be a street racing

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:53.059
crash during 2006's Fast and Furious: Tokyo
Drift, but Han's presence proved to be so

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:57.540
beloved by fans that the character was included
in the fourth, fifth, and sixth films.

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:02.170
The canonical timeline was rearranged so that
Tokyo Drift actually takes place after the

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:04.060
events of Fast &amp; Furious 6.

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:08.520
The mid-credits scene of Fast 6 shows the
exact scene from Tokyo Drift in which Han

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:12.520
dies, but reveals the crash to be an intentional
act by Deckard Shaw.

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:18.100
Since Han's death and the later rehabilitation
of Deckard as a good guy, the hashtag JusticeforHan

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:20.440
became popular online for two reasons.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:24.939
One, the character is deeply missed and two,
because it's more than a little unfair that

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:27.200
his killer is now buddy-buddy with Team Dom.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:31.180
"Justice is coming" according to the trailer,
and we couldn't be more excited.

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:36.520
We couldn't be happier to see that Helen Mirren
is reprising her role as Magdalene Shaw once

00:01:36.539 --> 00:01:40.639
again after the character first appeared in
Fate of the Furious, and then cameoed in Hobbs

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:41.260
&amp; Shaw.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:45.499
If you missed her most recent appearance in
Hobbs &amp; Shaw, you might not know that Magdalene

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:48.960
was sprung out of prison by Deckard and Hattie,
two of her three children.

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:54.159
Unfortunately, due to the productions of Hobbs
&amp; Shaw and F9 overlapping, neither Deckard

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:56.380
nor Hattie will be joining the team in F9.

00:01:56.660 --> 00:02:00.700
Their new Best Friend Forever, Dwayne Johnson's
Luke Hobbs, will likewise not be appearing

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:01.520
in F9.

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:04.140
Owen Shaw, however, might be a different story.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:09.160
Originally the major antagonist of Fast 6,
Owen ended up in a hospital after Dom's crew

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:10.080
did a number on him.

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:14.560
That stay in the hospital was what originally
motivated big brother Deckard to kill Han

00:02:14.569 --> 00:02:18.849
and swear vengeance on Dom's Family, before
ultimately breaking bread with them in Fate

00:02:18.849 --> 00:02:19.800
of the Furious.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:24.550
The writers for Fast and Furious 9 have obliquely
teased that Owen might be ready to rumble

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:29.180
again beyond his brief cameo in Fate of the
Furious, though they didn't specify when.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:34.060
It's entirely possible he'll skip ahead to
appear in Fast and the Furious 10 instead,

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:35.620
which is already in pre production.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:39.599
Still, his possible appearance is something
to keep in mind as the story revs up.

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:45.080
As the F9 trailer reveals, Dom and Mia Toretto
have a secret brother now: Jakob.

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:48.930
In fact, director Justin Lin is returning
to the franchise after sitting out for the

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:53.099
seventh and eighth films precisely because
he wanted to invert the trope of found family

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:54.620
in the Fast and Furious franchise.

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:56.260
As he told Entertainment Weekly:

00:02:56.660 --> 00:03:00.880
"When I left after Fast 6, I really thought
that was it, like, there's no more Fast stories

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:01.580
I can tell.

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:04.660
Then two years ago, I woke up with an idea
for the new chapter.

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:09.120
And a big part of that is exploring this theme
of family that is always tied to Fast, but

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:10.270
doing it through blood."

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:13.020
"You don't turn your back on family.

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:16.440
Even when they do."

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:21.280
Given all the new familial surprises in F9,
it looks like there's never been a better

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:25.569
time for Dom's sister Mia Toretto to make
a full return to the front lines of the Fast

00:03:25.569 --> 00:03:26.200
franchise.

00:03:26.689 --> 00:03:31.420
We last saw Mia in action back in Fast and
Furious 6, but she took a backseat in Furious

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:33.080
7 due to her second pregnancy.

00:03:33.349 --> 00:03:37.099
Rather than battle super spies, she stayed
in the Dominican Republic while the rest of

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:39.280
the Family drove cars through skyscrapers.

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:44.820
Things became complicated following the sudden
and tragic death of Paul Walker in 2013, halfway

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:46.680
through production of Furious 7.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:51.099
An entire coda was added to the end of the
film to celebrate Walker's life through his

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:54.880
character Brian and his relationship to Mia
as part of the overarching story.

00:03:55.409 --> 00:03:59.099
Since Mia's character is so entwined with
Brian, she didn't appear in Fate of the Furious

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:02.840
under the guise of the two wanting a quieter,
safer life with their children.

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:08.020
The entire franchise has had a period of readjustment
since Walker's loss, and Mia's place within

00:04:08.029 --> 00:04:11.510
canon represents the biggest challenge of
all: how do you write around the fact that

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:15.360
Mia gets to go back on big, superheroic car
adventures and Brian doesn't?

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:20.019
Apparently the answer involves giving her
and Dom a secret thief-slash-assassin brother

00:04:20.020 --> 00:04:21.340
played by John Cena.

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:26.860
This bombastic trailer has plenty of details
to pore over, but it's definitely not revealing

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:27.360
everything.

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:30.040
For one thing, Michael Rooker is nowhere to
be found.

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:34.060
The veteran character actor was confirmed
to be joining the cast way back in August

00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:34.880
2019.

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:39.120
It's odd that an actor enjoying a nice career
high thanks to the Marvel Cinematic Universe

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:41.850
wasn't featured in a trailer for another massive
franchise.

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:46.400
All we know for certain is that his character's
name is Buddy, and that Rooker was cast in

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:48.620
the last minute as production set to begin.

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:53.160
Considering the timing, it's possible he replaced
an actor whose availability suddenly fell

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:53.860
through.

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:55.850
From there, we can only speculate.

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:58.400
Will he be playing Dom, Mia, and Jakob's father?

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:01.700
Some sort of new henchman to Charlize Theron's
villainous Cypher?

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:06.160
Or maybe he'll simply be a helpful car mechanic
to get the Fast Family back on the road.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:07.440
One thing's for sure though:

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:13.040
"Have you ever heard the saying 'the enemy
of my enemy is my friend?'"

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:16.840
"I don't got friends, I got family."

